# CLAUDE CODE OFFLOAD WINDOW (CURSOR USAGE)

## Active period

- **Through:** end of day **April 5, 2026** (matches Ryan’s **Claude / Anthropic membership** end date — if that date changes, update this file).
- **Purpose:** Preserve **Cursor** **Auto + Composer** and **API** pools until the **April 16** Cursor billing reset (and beyond) by running **everything reasonable** in **Claude Code Desktop** instead of long **Cursor Agent** sessions.

## Priority vs other rules

- This window is **specific** to tool routing. If it conflicts with generic defaults, follow **`claude-code-offload-window.mdc`** for **where execution runs**, while **content quality gates** (schema, TinyStories, safety, `claude-pro-sprint.mdc` locks) still apply.

## Default routing

| Do in **Claude Code Desktop** (project folder open) | Keep in **Cursor** (thin / Cursor-only) |
|-----------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------|
| Multi-file features, refactors, wide search-and-replace | **Scaffolding:** prompt shells, empty sections, paths, “paste block” headers in `docs/` |
| Long agentic coding sessions (“implement X across the repo”) | **Ask** / **Plan** questions, short strategy answers |
| Bulk JSON / prose / scripts (same as sprint policy) | **Validation** after Claude writes files: JSON parse, lint, schema checks |
| Anchor’s Desk / other repos when that is the active task | **Debug with AI** on red terminal errors (uses Cursor’s bundled context) |
| Heavy exploration when it would burn Cursor pools | **Review with AI** on Source Control diffs before commit |
| | Single-file **micro-edits** when faster than context-switching |
| | Tab autocomplete, `@Codebase` quick lookups with **Gemini Flash** when needed |

## Quality bar (no product downgrade)

- Offloading **does not** skip: **definition of done**, **lint**, the project's **content checklists**, **human editor** gates, or **device test** rules when code changed.
- Claude Code output is treated like any external output: **review**, **merge**, **verify** in Cursor or CI as already documented.

## Model hint (Claude Code)

- Default **Sonnet** for most coding; **Opus** for hardest bugs / architecture when worth the cost. Ryan picks in Claude Code.

## After the window ends (maintenance)

- On or after **2026-04-06:** set **`alwaysApply`** to **`false`** in this file **or** delete this rule file; refresh **`docs/CURSOR_MODEL_AND_MODE_REFERENCE.md`** (remove or close the offload section); routing returns to **`.cursor/rules/model-routing.mdc`** and **`claude-pro-sprint.mdc`** only.
